    {
      "id": "nse-weekend-sessions",
      "title": "NSE circulars on live trading sessions held on a Saturday or Sunday (2012-2026)",
      "publisher": "National Stock Exchange of India Limited",
      "location": "https://www.nseindia.com/resources/exchange-communication-circulars",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-15",
      "covers": "2010-02-06 to 2026-02-01",
      "notes": "Shortened 'special live trading sessions' with a separate settlement, held to bring a new trading system or the BCP site into live use: 6 February 2010 11:00-12:30 (NSE/CMTR/14051); 7 January, 3 March, 28 April and 8 September 2012, 11 May 2013 and 22 March 2014 (BCP site), each 11:15-12:45 (NSE/CMTR/19734, 20063, 20561, 21547, 23302, 26045); found from the exchange's circular index after the bhavcopy record showed trading on those Saturdays. Full regular sessions (09:15-15:30) on the Union Budget days 28 February 2015 (NSE/CMTR/28939), 1 February 2020 (43290, F&O twin FAOP/43291), 1 February 2025 (65729, NSE/MSD/66381) and Sunday 1 February 2026 (72349), and on Saturday 20 January 2024, when the planned disaster-recovery drill (NSE/MSD/59999, 60300; clearing NSE/CMPT/60016, 60026) became a regular session from the primary site (NSE/MSD/60340). Two-window sessions with an intra-day switch to the DR site on Saturdays 2 March 2024 (NSE/MSD/60677, reminder 60942) and 18 May 2024 (NSE/MSD/61893, F&O FAOP/62001): normal market 09:15-10:00 from the primary site and 11:30-12:30 from the DR site, with settlement. The Sunday sessions of 16 May 2010 (Akshaya Tritiya, 09:00-15:30, seven gold ETFs; NSE/CMTR/14775) and 11 November 2012 (Dhanteras, 11:00-15:30, gold ETFs; NSE/CMTR/22063) were limited to gold ETFs and are not modelled.",
